1
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,284
[HOST] In the summer of 1985,

2
00:00:24,284 --> 00:00:28,020
a record-breaking heatwave scorched
the roads across California,

3
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,413
yet the atmosphere across the city of Los

4
00:00:30,413 --> 00:00:33,040
Angeles was gripped by
a bone-chilling dread.

5
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:37,503
Despite the stifling heat, millions
of residents bolted their windows,

6
00:00:37,503 --> 00:00:40,800
locked their doors, and spent
sleepless nights in sheer terror.

7
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:45,091
An invisible phantom was breaking
into homes in the dead of night,

8
00:00:45,091 --> 00:00:47,470
adhering to no discernible
pattern or boundary.

9
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,500
His victims spanned every age
group and social demographic,

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,950
ranging from young couples to
elderly individuals living alone.

11
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,953
A wave of collective paranoia
swept through the metropolis,

12
00:00:58,953 --> 00:01:01,023
turning homes that should have been safe

13
00:01:01,023 --> 00:01:03,300
havens into claustrophobic
traps of anxiety.

14
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:08,029
The press bestowed upon the nocturnal
killer a terrifying moniker:

15
00:01:08,029 --> 00:01:09,100
The Night Stalker.

16
00:01:10,050 --> 00:01:12,335
It became one of the
largest and most breathless

17
00:01:12,335 --> 00:01:14,810
manhunts in the history of
American law enforcement.

18
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,097
[HOST] Unlike conventional
serial killers who

19
00:01:18,097 --> 00:01:20,345
typically target a specific demographic,

20
00:01:20,345 --> 00:01:24,000
the Night Stalker operated with
utter chaos and unpredictability.

21
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,504
He never viewed his victims as human
beings endowed with life and family,

22
00:01:28,504 --> 00:01:32,360
but degraded them into props for his
thirst for dominance and dark violence.

23
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:36,947
He entered homes randomly through
unlocked windows and occasionally

24
00:01:36,947 --> 00:01:40,150
left bizarre inverted pentagram
symbols at the crime scene.

25
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:43,386
Sales of firearms, home security systems,

26
00:01:43,386 --> 00:01:46,238
and door deadbolts across
California skyrocketed

27
00:01:46,238 --> 00:01:49,150
in an unprecedented frenzy
to protect loved ones.

28
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:52,587
Under the command of two
veteran detectives from

29
00:01:52,587 --> 00:01:54,867
the Los Angeles County
Sheriff's Department,

30
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:57,509
Detective Gil Carrillo and
Detective Frank Salerno,

31
00:01:57,509 --> 00:02:00,100
thousands of leads were
scrutinized day and night.

32
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,896
The decisive breakthrough arrived when

33
00:02:02,896 --> 00:02:05,313
investigators recovered
a single viable latent

34
00:02:05,313 --> 00:02:09,620
fingerprint from a stolen orange Toyota
station wagon that the suspect had driven.

35
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:14,834
California's newly deployed Automated
Fingerprint Identification System,

36
00:02:14,834 --> 00:02:18,210
known as AFIS, achieved a
historic technological triumph.

37
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:23,187
Computer records instantly generated
a definitive match: Richard Ramirez,

38
00:02:23,187 --> 00:02:27,650
a twenty-five-year-old Texas native with
a prior criminal history of burglary.

39
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,678
[HOST] On the morning of
August 31, 1985, the stark,

40
00:02:31,678 --> 00:02:35,067
menacing face of Richard
Ramirez was plastered across

41
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:38,520
the front page of every major
newspaper in California.

42
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,406
At that exact moment,

43
00:02:40,406 --> 00:02:44,442
Ramirez had just disembarked from a bus
returning from Arizona to Los Angeles,

44
00:02:44,442 --> 00:02:47,960
completely oblivious that his mugshot
had been broadcast everywhere.

45
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:52,172
Walking into a neighborhood
convenience store in East Los Angeles,

46
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:55,830
he was stunned to see his own face
staring back at him from the newsstand.

47
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:59,546
In absolute panic, the predator
bolted into the street,

48
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:03,310
desperately attempting to carjack
passing motorists to make his escape.

49
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,095
Yet this time,

50
00:03:05,095 --> 00:03:07,837
the man who had terrorized
an entire state was

51
00:03:07,837 --> 00:03:10,937
forced to confront a force
he had never anticipated:

52
00:03:10,937 --> 00:03:13,620
The unified courage of
an outraged community.

53
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:17,833
Residents along Hubbard Street in
East Los Angeles raised the alarm

54
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:20,940
in unison and joined together
to pursue the fleeing predator.

55
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:24,190
Imagine the lived
experience of a neighborhood

56
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:26,090
resident during that historic morning.

57
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,518
[RESIDENT] That Saturday
morning was a day that I will

58
00:03:29,518 --> 00:03:31,670
never be able to forget
for the rest of my life.

59
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:36,606
When we heard the frantic screams of a
neighborhood woman who was being carjacked,

60
00:03:36,606 --> 00:03:38,910
everyone rushed out onto
the street immediately.

61
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:40,774
I saw a tall,

62
00:03:40,774 --> 00:03:43,412
gaunt man with hollow
cheeks running desperately

63
00:03:43,412 --> 00:03:45,500
through our narrow residential alleys.

64
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:50,220
A neighbor recognized that his face
was identical to the Night Stalker

65
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:54,100
mugshot printed on the morning front
page and shouted his identity aloud.

66
00:03:55,250 --> 00:03:55,880
Immediately,

67
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,610
dozens of men from throughout our
East Los Angeles neighborhood charged

68
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:03,130
out into the street to cut off his
escape route and chase him down.

69
00:04:04,130 --> 00:04:05,811
Our fear completely vanished,

70
00:04:05,811 --> 00:04:10,450
replaced by an absolute determination to
protect our families and our community.

71
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,079
Together,

72
00:04:12,079 --> 00:04:15,059
the residents pinned the
killer securely to the sidewalk

73
00:04:15,059 --> 00:04:17,720
until police cruisers
arrived with sirens wailing.

74
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:22,136
When the monster who had terrorized
California was finally subdued,

75
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:24,379
we knew that this summer
nightmare was ended

76
00:04:24,379 --> 00:04:26,520
by the sheer courage of ordinary citizens.

77
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:31,097
In that defining moment of pinning
the killer to the pavement,

78
00:04:31,097 --> 00:04:35,132
the paralyzing fear that had suffocated
us all summer dissolved entirely,

79
00:04:35,132 --> 00:04:38,670
replaced by profound pride in our
collective community strength.

80
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:43,452
We realized that when ordinary people
unite to protect what is right,

81
00:04:43,452 --> 00:04:47,070
no phantom of terror can ever hold
our neighborhood hostage again.

82
00:04:48,570 --> 00:04:52,384
[HOST] The public capture on the streets
of East Los Angeles on August 31,

83
00:04:52,384 --> 00:04:54,832
1985 officially brought
an end to the Night

84
00:04:54,832 --> 00:04:57,450
Stalker's reign of terror
lasting over a year.

85
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:00,474
When patrol officers arrived on the scene,

86
00:05:00,474 --> 00:05:03,334
Richard Ramirez had already
been completely restrained

87
00:05:03,334 --> 00:05:05,770
on the sidewalk by
courageous local residents.

88
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:09,355
Law enforcement officers
quickly formed a protective

89
00:05:09,355 --> 00:05:12,040
barrier and escorted him
away from the enraged crowd.

90
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,824
He was transported to police
headquarters under maximum

91
00:05:15,824 --> 00:05:19,080
security protocols to prepare
for interrogation proceedings.

92
00:05:20,030 --> 00:05:22,578
A breathless tactical
manhunt was concluded,

93
00:05:22,578 --> 00:05:26,110
ushering in an arduous legal
and psychological confrontation.

94
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:31,039
Yet what astonished investigators was not
merely the predator's outward arrogance,

95
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:33,910
but the twisted architecture
of his psychological makeup.

96
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,262
A complex and disturbed
psychological portrait

97
00:05:37,262 --> 00:05:39,820
began to emerge from behind
the veil of darkness.

98
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:43,530
Yet from another agonizing
perspective back in El Paso,

99
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:47,180
the news struck the perpetrator's
own family like a devastating blow.

100
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:50,634
They became the secondary
victims of the tragedy,

101
00:05:50,634 --> 00:05:53,752
condemned to live out their
remaining days under the crushing

102
00:05:53,752 --> 00:05:56,410
weight of familial guilt
and harsh social ostracism.

103
00:05:57,910 --> 00:06:01,291
[INVESTIGATOR] Imagine an investigator
sitting across from Richard Ramirez

104
00:06:01,291 --> 00:06:04,270
for the very first time in
an interrogation chamber.

105
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:07,795
He carried himself with
chilling arrogance,

106
00:06:07,795 --> 00:06:12,230
eyes flashing with open defiance and
completely devoid of any remorse.

107
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,135
Later in court,

108
00:06:14,135 --> 00:06:17,062
he would raise a hand
branded with a pentagram

109
00:06:17,062 --> 00:06:20,180
and utter occult slogans
to provoke public shock.

110
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:23,359
From a behavioral science perspective,

111
00:06:23,359 --> 00:06:26,990
Ramirez represented an extremely
dangerous mixed offender,

112
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:31,060
combining disorganized impulsivity
with cunning forensic evasion.

113
00:06:32,010 --> 00:06:35,865
He utilized occult dogma as a
moral disengagement mechanism

114
00:06:35,865 --> 00:06:39,850
to anesthetize his conscience
and rationalize his atrocities.

115
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,159
However,

116
00:06:41,159 --> 00:06:43,769
what shocked the investigative task force

117
00:06:43,769 --> 00:06:46,570
most was not his brazen
behavior in custody.

118
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:50,620
The true shock lay in the
surreal reaction of a segment of

119
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:53,880
the public outside the courtroom
in the months that followed.

120
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:59,029
[HOST] The arrest of Richard Ramirez
seemed poised to bring complete peace

121
00:06:59,029 --> 00:07:02,460
and absolute societal unanimity
in condemning unvarnished evil.

122
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:07,068
Yet as the formal trial commenced
at the Los Angeles Superior Court,

123
00:07:07,068 --> 00:07:10,260
an unprecedented and grotesque
social phenomenon erupted.

124
00:07:11,210 --> 00:07:13,693
It marked the emergence
of a morbid wave of

125
00:07:13,693 --> 00:07:16,118
infatuation directed at the serial killer,

126
00:07:16,118 --> 00:07:18,370
scientifically known as Hybristophilia.

127
00:07:19,170 --> 00:07:22,422
A mirror reflecting deep
cognitive blindspots and distorted

128
00:07:22,422 --> 00:07:25,730
emotional needs in modern society
was about to be laid bare.

129
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:30,204
[HOST] The trial of Richard Ramirez,

130
00:07:30,204 --> 00:07:33,379
spanning jury selection in
1988 to the verdict in 1989,

131
00:07:33,379 --> 00:07:38,170
became one of the most bizarre and chaotic
spectacles in American judicial history.

132
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:41,566
Alongside incontrovertible
forensic evidence and

133
00:07:41,566 --> 00:07:44,215
heart-wrenching testimony
from surviving victims,

134
00:07:44,215 --> 00:07:47,730
the courtroom air was constantly
disrupted by a jarring presence.

135
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:52,546
Scores of young women dressed in
black attire and heavy makeup lined up

136
00:07:52,546 --> 00:07:56,520
before dawn merely to secure spectator
seats and gaze upon the defendant.

137
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:59,032
They exchanged adoring glances,

138
00:07:59,032 --> 00:08:02,069
whispering among themselves
and regarding the nocturnal

139
00:08:02,069 --> 00:08:04,720
murderer as a brooding
icon of rebellious charm.

140
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:09,073
This media circus created a
bitter contrast between the solemn

141
00:08:09,073 --> 00:08:12,750
dignity of the law and the profound
deviance of courtroom groupies.

142
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:16,237
[HOST] Despite facing
charges for thirteen murders

143
00:08:16,237 --> 00:08:19,010
alongside dozens of severe
assaults and burglaries,

144
00:08:19,010 --> 00:08:22,380
Ramirez was treated by his
admirers like an elusive rock star.

145
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:27,405
He swaggered into the courtroom sporting
dark sunglasses, unkempt dark hair,

146
00:08:27,405 --> 00:08:30,740
and a sneering smirk that openly
mocked the civilized world.

147
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:34,686
Every subtle gesture or
indifferent glance was watched with

148
00:08:34,686 --> 00:08:37,530
breathless fascination by
young women seated behind him.

149
00:08:38,330 --> 00:08:39,240
Every single day,

150
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,185
Ramirez received hundreds of
romantic love letters sent

151
00:08:42,185 --> 00:08:44,970
to his holding facility
from women he had never met.

152
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,668
Many enclosed personal
photographs and expressed a

153
00:08:48,668 --> 00:08:51,526
naive conviction that he
was merely a misunderstood,

154
00:08:51,526 --> 00:08:52,240
wounded soul.

155
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:56,827
This represented a textbook
manifestation of the reverse halo effect,

156
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:59,846
where chiseled physical
features were blindly conflated

157
00:08:59,846 --> 00:09:02,480
with rugged masculinity
and misunderstood depth.

158
00:09:03,430 --> 00:09:05,945
That grotesque spectacle
carved deep wounds into the

159
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:08,750
grieving families of the victims
present in the courtroom.

160
00:09:09,550 --> 00:09:12,104
They were forced to watch the
predator who had shattered

161
00:09:12,104 --> 00:09:14,750
their families being glorified
inside the hall of justice.

162
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:19,676
The morbid frenzy of this devoted
fanbase created a cruel moral paradox

163
00:09:19,676 --> 00:09:23,540
right before the eyes of the surviving
victims and grieving families.

164
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:28,326
They were forced to swallow their
agonizing grief as the man who destroyed

165
00:09:28,326 --> 00:09:32,420
their lives was celebrated like a
mythical icon in the sensationalist press.

166
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:37,943
[INVESTIGATOR] Imagine the visceral disgust
experienced by seasoned investigators

167
00:09:37,943 --> 00:09:41,600
watching a fan base fawn over
Ramirez inside a court of law.

168
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:46,069
Those women appeared completely
blind to the gruesome reality of

169
00:09:46,069 --> 00:09:49,680
the crimes and the irreparable
grief of the surviving families.

170
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:54,978
They glorified a cowardly prowler who
had crept through windows in the dark,

171
00:09:54,978 --> 00:09:57,267
attacking innocent people in their beds,

172
00:09:57,267 --> 00:10:00,070
simply because of his
posturing before the press.

173
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:02,886
From an investigative reality,

174
00:10:02,886 --> 00:10:06,043
Ramirez was never an
enigmatic dark prince or a

175
00:10:06,043 --> 00:10:09,470
romantic antihero concocted
by sensational fiction.

176
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,290
He was a petty,

177
00:10:11,290 --> 00:10:14,305
cowardly predator who
specifically targeted the most

178
00:10:14,305 --> 00:10:17,900
vulnerable individuals when their
defenses were entirely down.

179
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,511
The burning question remains:

180
00:10:20,511 --> 00:10:24,256
What psychological mechanism
drove otherwise ordinary people

181
00:10:24,256 --> 00:10:27,940
to venerate and profess affection
for such a brutal killer?

182
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:32,130
The answer does not lie
in simple infatuation,

183
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:36,940
but within profound cognitive distortions
and complex emotional delusions.

184
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:37,965
Yet,

185
00:10:37,965 --> 00:10:41,797
it was the unyielding courage of
the surviving victims stepping onto

186
00:10:41,797 --> 00:10:45,460
the witness stand that ultimately
shattered that arrogant facade.

187
00:10:46,410 --> 00:10:49,192
By looking straight into
the killer's eyes and

188
00:10:49,192 --> 00:10:51,974
raising their voices to
expose his atrocities,

189
00:10:51,974 --> 00:10:56,450
they stripped away his dark mystique
to reclaim justice and human dignity.

190
00:10:57,950 --> 00:11:00,737
[HOST] Among the women
captivated by the Night Stalker,

191
00:11:00,737 --> 00:11:04,163
the most notorious and public
case was that of Doreen Lioy,

192
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,950
an educated woman and
freelance magazine editor.

193
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:10,820
Defying fierce condemnation
from her family and society,

194
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:14,055
Lioy faithfully wrote seventy-five
letters to Ramirez while

195
00:11:14,055 --> 00:11:17,070
he was housed on death row
at San Quentin State Prison.

196
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:21,101
She claimed that Ramirez was
an affectionate, charming man,

197
00:11:21,101 --> 00:11:24,860
insisting she could see a pure and
saintly core buried within his being.

198
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:26,823
On October 3, 1996,

199
00:11:26,823 --> 00:11:30,373
Doreen Lioy officially married
the convicted serial killer

200
00:11:30,373 --> 00:11:33,740
inside the visitation room
of San Quentin State Prison.

201
00:11:34,690 --> 00:11:38,293
Lioy wore a gold wedding band and
proudly proclaimed to the media that

202
00:11:38,293 --> 00:11:42,050
her love would serve as a transformative
sanctuary for the condemned man.

203
00:11:42,850 --> 00:11:44,970
This marriage, which endured for years,

204
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:48,450
became a classic case study in
the depths of the savior complex.

205
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:52,579
It provided unmistakable proof
of how thoroughly irrational

206
00:11:52,579 --> 00:11:55,920
beliefs can warp perception when
personal boundaries collapse.

207
00:11:57,420 --> 00:12:00,773
[INVESTIGATOR] Regardless of the
media circus created by spectators,

208
00:12:00,773 --> 00:12:05,580
the justice system remained unyielding
in its commitment to objective truth.

209
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:11,100
Prosecutors presented the jury with an
airtight mountain of physical evidence:

210
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,311
latent fingerprints,

211
00:12:12,311 --> 00:12:15,639
distinctive size eleven and
a half Avia sneaker tracks,

212
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:18,060
and courageous testimony from survivors.

213
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:23,724
The modus operandi of the perpetrator
demonstrated cunning premeditation:

214
00:12:23,724 --> 00:12:27,082
severing telephone wires,
striking in dead of night,

215
00:12:27,082 --> 00:12:29,730
and constantly changing getaway vehicles.

216
00:12:30,530 --> 00:12:32,917
Meanwhile, his psychological signature,

217
00:12:32,917 --> 00:12:35,978
from inverted pentagrams
scrawled on bedroom walls

218
00:12:35,978 --> 00:12:38,671
to rummaging through
victims' refrigerators,

219
00:12:38,671 --> 00:12:42,650
proved a pathological craving for
power and absolute subjugation.

220
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:47,237
No amount of courtroom
romanticization or occult theatrics

221
00:12:47,237 --> 00:12:51,000
could disguise the cold reality
of calculated serial murder.

222
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:55,905
On September 20, 1989,
following arduous deliberations,

223
00:12:55,905 --> 00:13:01,353
the jury found Richard Ramirez guilty
on all forty-three criminal counts,

224
00:13:01,353 --> 00:13:04,040
including thirteen counts of murder.

225
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,805
[HOST] The death penalty
handed down by Judge

226
00:13:07,805 --> 00:13:10,129
Michael Tynan in November 1989 formally

227
00:13:10,129 --> 00:13:14,420
concluded the Night Stalker's reign
of terror before the bar of justice.

228
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,828
In his formal pronouncement,

229
00:13:16,828 --> 00:13:20,101
Judge Tynan emphasized that
Ramirez's acts demonstrated a

230
00:13:20,101 --> 00:13:23,260
cruelty and callousness beyond
any human comprehension.

231
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:29,081
Confronting the ultimate legal penalty,
Ramirez maintained a mask of insolence,

232
00:13:29,081 --> 00:13:32,410
sneering a defiant catchphrase:
See you in Disneyland.

233
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:36,043
That arrogant parting shot
was not genuine bravado,

234
00:13:36,043 --> 00:13:39,099
but pathological self-pity
and the defensive bluster of

235
00:13:39,099 --> 00:13:42,210
a narcissist who could not
stomach his own total defeat.

236
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:45,946
The killer was transported
to San Quentin State Prison,

237
00:13:45,946 --> 00:13:50,200
