with ordinary human empathy.

309
00:17:45,150 --> 00:17:48,854
Yet what stunned academia was not
merely the etiology of his crimes,

310
00:17:48,854 --> 00:17:51,251
but the psychological
phenomenon manifesting

311
00:17:51,251 --> 00:17:53,430
on the other side of the courtroom rail.

312
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:57,568
The phenomenon of women becoming
romantically enamored with

313
00:17:57,568 --> 00:18:01,026
violent offenders is scientifically
cataloged as Hybristophilia,

314
00:18:01,026 --> 00:18:03,620
colloquially known as
Bonnie and Clyde Syndrome.

315
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:08,248
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The term Hybristophilia
derives from ancient Greek,

316
00:18:08,248 --> 00:18:09,352
uniting hybrizein,

317
00:18:09,352 --> 00:18:14,320
meaning to commit an outrage, with philia,
denoting intense passionate affection.

318
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,514
In forensic psychiatry,

319
00:18:16,514 --> 00:18:20,939
it is classified as a paraphilic
emotional fixation wherein an individual

320
00:18:20,939 --> 00:18:25,000
is intensely aroused by someone
who has committed heinous violence.

321
00:18:25,950 --> 00:18:30,151
Researchers divide this syndrome into
two distinct operational subtypes:

322
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:33,710
The aggressive active variant
and the passive savior variant.

323
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:38,498
In the aggressive active variant, the
woman becomes an active accomplice,

324
00:18:38,498 --> 00:18:42,157
assisting in harboring or facilitating
the partner's criminal acts,

325
00:18:42,157 --> 00:18:44,670
as demonstrated historically
by Bonnie Parker.

326
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:46,256
Conversely,

327
00:18:46,256 --> 00:18:49,433
the vast majority of women
drawn to Richard Ramirez and

328
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:52,900
similar serial killers belong
to the passive savior subtype.

329
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:58,473
This cohort is driven by a deep cognitive
trap known as the Savior Delusion,

330
00:18:58,473 --> 00:18:59,980
or Can-Fix-Him Syndrome.

331
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:04,462
They nurture a naive yet fierce
conviction that their pure devotion

332
00:19:04,462 --> 00:19:07,730
can rehabilitate and redeem the
tormented soul of the monster.

333
00:19:08,530 --> 00:19:12,890
They rationalize that the killer is only
savage toward a cruel outside world,

334
00:19:12,890 --> 00:19:16,570
while remaining gentle, misunderstood,
and devoted to them alone.

335
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:21,724
This defense mechanism enables them to
completely disassociate from the horrific

336
00:19:21,724 --> 00:19:25,560
reality of the devastation the
perpetrator inflicted on innocent victims.

337
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:29,713
It represents pathological
cognitive compartmentalization,

338
00:19:29,713 --> 00:19:34,280
where an idealized romantic fantasy is
completely severed from objective truth.

339
00:19:35,230 --> 00:19:38,316
The savior complex plunged
these women into an extreme

340
00:19:38,316 --> 00:19:41,630
state of cognitive
compartmentalization to escape reality.

341
00:19:42,430 --> 00:19:44,663
They imprisoned themselves in a delusional

342
00:19:44,663 --> 00:19:46,896
psychological sanctuary where romanticized

343
00:19:46,896 --> 00:19:50,830
fantasies were worshiped at the dreadful
cost of dishonoring the deceased.

344
00:19:52,330 --> 00:19:56,357
[HOST] The fantasy of becoming the sole
redeemer for a man condemned by the entire

345
00:19:56,357 --> 00:20:00,170
world endowed these women with an
intoxicating illusion of omnipotence.

346
00:20:00,970 --> 00:20:05,153
It served as a colossal source of narcissistic
supply for personalities grappling

347
00:20:05,153 --> 00:20:09,130
